-- title:
--   Uniqueness of deformation lifts along a small extension
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ (adically complete for its maximal ideal) whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative one-dimensional formal group law over $k$ admitting a Drinfeld basis in the sense of `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with the zero ideal as ambient ideal there is a unit $u \in k[[X]]$ with $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ q = u \cdot F_0.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\ q\ 0\ 0$; let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$. Assume the universal property `hFu1`: for every artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, satisfying $(\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\ T)^2 = 0$ and $q = 0$ in $T$, and every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ reducing to $F_0$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ for which the coefficientwise image of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ is isomorphic, by a `LawIso` whose series reduces to $X$ modulo the maximal ideal, to $G$. Now let $T$ and $S$ be artinian local $W_0$-algebras with compatible surjections $\mathrm{res}_T$, $\mathrm{res}_S$ onto $k$ with kernels the maximal ideals, and let $\sigma : T \to S$ be a surjective $W_0$-algebra map with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \sigma = \mathrm{res}_T$ and $(\ker \sigma) \cdot \mathrm{maximalIdeal}\ T = 0$. Let $G$ be a commutative formal group law over $T$ reducing to $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, and $G_\sigma$ its image over $S$ along $\sigma$. Let $\bar\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to S$ be a $W_0$-algebra map with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \bar\varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, let $\bar{G}'$ be the image of $F_u$ along $\bar\varphi$, and let $\bar\psi : \bar{G}' \to G_\sigma$ be an isomorphism of formal group laws whose series has coefficients reducing to those of $X$. Finally let $\varphi_1, \varphi_2 : W_0[[X]] \to T$ be $W_0$-algebra maps with $\sigma \circ \varphi_i = \bar\varphi$, each equipped with the image $G_i'$ of $F_u$ along $\varphi_i$ and an isomorphism $\psi_i : G_i' \to G$ whose series reduces to $X$ modulo the maximal ideal of $T$. The conclusion is $\varphi_1 = \varphi_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the inductive small-extension step in the deformation theory of a height-two formal group law with Drinfeld basis data, in the style of Schlessinger's criteria: lifts of a given $W_0$-algebra map along a small surjection $T \to S$, when equipped with the corresponding trivialised isomorphism to $G$, are unique. It feeds the existence-and-uniqueness statement [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.existsUnique_algHom_powerSeries_lift_of_smallExtension_of_sqZero`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.existsUnique_algHom_powerSeries_lift_of_smallExtension_of_sqZero), and it uses the rigidity result [`FormalGroup.LawHom.series_eq_of_map_series_eq_of_surjective_of_ker_pow_eq_bot`](thm.html#FormalGroup.LawHom.series_eq_of_map_series_eq_of_surjective_of_ker_pow_eq_bot) for homomorphism series over rings whose residue ideal is nilpotent of bounded order.
